; A DECLARED NOMINAL RESULT OVER A BARE `Int` BODY - the handle
; convention run backwards, and a SIGSEGV that `check` called OK.
;
; `Int` is this language's universal heap handle. A signature saying
; `Int` over a body that answers a `Span` is that convention working:
; the caller receives a word and nothing generated from the signature
; dereferences it. `498-param-through-int.ax` carves the one exception.
;
; The REVERSE has no convention behind it. A signature saying `Box`
; over a body that answers an `Int` hands the caller a word the caller
; WILL dereference, because the declaration told it that is safe - a
; `match` emits a tag load from the address. Measured on 0.6.0
; (`9116167`), a compiler built from that tree:
;
;   (:: g (-> Int Box))  (fn (g x) 7)
;   (fn (main) (match (g 1) ((Bx s) (strLen s))))
;
;   axiom check  ->  OK, exit 0
;   axiom run    ->  exit 139, SIGSEGV, no output
;
; The SAME mismatch in ARGUMENT position was AX3004 the whole time -
; `(h 7)` against `(:: h (-> Box Int))` - so the rule existed and was
; applied in one position out of two. `tyReprClash` is a NAME list
; (`Bool`, `Float`, `Foreign`, `Handle`, `String`), and a name list
; catches only the names on it: every `data`, every `struct`, every
; `Char`, list, tuple and lambda went through it, in the one direction
; that segfaults. `checkDeclaredReturn` now compares by `tyCompat`
; unless the DECLARED side is a bare `Int`.
;
;   line 49: the reproducer above - a `data` handle minted from 7
;   line 53: a `struct` handle minted from a parameter
;   line 57: two nominal types punned, which no name list could reach
;
; The three controls draw nothing, and each is load-bearing:
;   `mkSpan`  the handle convention itself - 29 sites in this tree
;             return a handle through a declared `Int`, and every one
;             of them must stay accepted
;   `mkOk`    `(cast Box n)`, the explicit escape, which is what a
;             function that really does mint a handle from a word says
;   `unwrap`  the honest direction, so the case is not vacuous
(import Str)

(data Box (Bx String))

(struct Pt (x : Int) (y : Int))

(:: g (-> Int Box))

(fn (g x) 7)

(:: mkPt (-> Int Pt))

(fn (mkPt n) n)

(:: pun (-> Int Box))

(fn (pun n) (Pt n n))

(:: mkSpan (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (mkSpan a b) (Pt a b))

(:: mkOk (-> Int Box))

(fn (mkOk n) (cast Box n))

(:: unwrap (-> Box Int))

(fn (unwrap b)
  (match b
    ((Bx s) (strLen s))
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (unwrap (g 1)))
